s/Copilot/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jsurrea/aima-visualizations/commits/cf1fee691e3961156fbbf18bc72d7415971f4344/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-05T03:48:14Z","email":"198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"copilot-swe-agent[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-05T03:48:14Z","email":"198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"copilot-swe-agent[bot]"},"message":"chapter-14: implement probabilistic reasoning over time algorithms\n\nImplement all §14.2–14.5 algorithms with 100% branch + line coverage.\n\nsrc/algorithms/index.ts:\n- All TypeScript interfaces (HMMParams, FilterStep, SmoothStep,\n  ViterbiStep/Result, KalmanStep1D/2D, KalmanParams1D/2D,\n  Particle, ParticleFilterStep)\n- Matrix helpers: normalize, matMul, matTranspose, matInverse2x2,\n  matInverse (Gauss–Jordan with partial pivoting), matAdd, matSub,\n  matScale, matVecMul, outerProduct, identityMatrix\n- HMM: hmmForward (§14.2.1), hmmBackward (§14.2.2),\n  forwardBackward (§14.2.2), viterbi (§14.2.3)\n- Kalman: kalmanFilter1D (§14.4.2), kalmanFilter2D (§14.4.3)\n- Particle filter: particleFilter with seeded Mulberry32 PRNG (§14.5.3)\n- All pure functions; noUncheckedIndexedAccess uses ! assertions\n  (not ?? 0) to avoid phantom uncovered branches in V8 coverage\n\ntests/algorithms.test.ts:\n- 74 tests, 100% branch/line/function/statement coverage\n- Umbrella world: P(R1|u1)≈[0.818,0.182], P(R2|u1,u2)≈[0.883,0.117]\n- Smoothing: P(R1|u1,u2)≈[0.883,0.117]\n- Viterbi [T,T,F,T,T] → [R,R,¬R,R,R] (book answer §14.2.3)\n- Kalman 1D analytic ground truth (K=2/3, posterior=2/3 for z=1)\n- Kalman 2D equivalence with 1D scalar case\n- Particle filter: seeded reproducibility, valid state indices,\n  belief sums to 1\n- All matrix helpers, edge cases, singular matrix throws\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","