3341420a437115e15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/commits/a2643202112b26617d581bb3341420a437115e15"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18365190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JReque","id":18365190,"login":"JReque","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzY1MTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/commits/48ea9bbf9fbd9835895b60f7f9d0ab9421846093/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T04:04:27Z","email":"jrequena9@gmail.com","name":"Jesus Requena"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T04:04:27Z","email":"jrequena9@gmail.com","name":"Jesus Requena"},"message":"fix(table): keep focus and scroll coherent while windowing (F3)\n\nTwo defects the virtualization tests surfaced, plus the documented\nlimits of windowing.\n\nFocus. The assumption going in was that scrolling destroys the focused\ncontrol and drops focus to the body. It usually does not: Lit reuses the\nrow''s DOM positionally and rebinds it, so the focused chevron survives\nand now represents a DIFFERENT record. A keyboard or screen reader user\nbelieves they are on row 5 while they are on row 505, with nothing\nannounced — quieter than losing focus, and worse. Focus is now tracked\nby the record''s `aria-rowindex`, and when the window moves it off that\nrecord it is parked on the scroll container. Guarded so an unrelated\nre-render, a Tab-away, or focus leaving the component never triggers it.\n\nScroll. Shrinking the dataset (a filter, a refetch) while parked near\nthe bottom leaves the offset past the end of the new content. The\nbrowser clamps its own `scrollTop` but emits no scroll event, so the\ntracked `_scrollTop` kept describing a position that no longer existed\nand the window rendered a slice past the end — four rows out of five,\nwith the first ones stranded above the viewport. Clamp explicitly and\nresync from the container either way.\n\nAlso gives expand rows the `aria-rowindex` of the record they belong to,\nso they are not extra rows outside the declared `aria-rowcount`.\n\nDocuments what windowing costs regardless of implementation: find-in-page\ncannot reach unrendered rows, only rendered rows are in the tab order,\nand `rowHeight` is a contract the consumer has to honor.","tree":{"sha":"05e0f4462a90309361064857314a4f8b344ed0d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/git/trees/05e0f4462a90309361064857314a4f8b344ed0d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/git/commits/48ea9bbf9fbd9835895b60f7f9d0ab9421846093","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18365190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JReque","id":18365190,"login":"JReque","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzY1MTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/JReque/reke-ui/commit/48ea9bbf9fbd9835895b60f7f9d0ab9421846093","node_id":"C_kwDORd369doAKDQ4ZWE5YmJmOWZiZDk4MzU4OTViNjBmN2Y5ZDBhYjk0MjE4NDYwOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/JReque/reke-ui/commit/250e55a0cff6e69fdd0194a8ee4bff4ed7bb6833","sha":"250e55a0cff6e69fdd0194a8ee4bff4ed7bb6833","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/commits/250e55a0cff6e69fdd0194a8ee4bff4ed7bb6833"}],"sha":"48ea9bbf9fbd9835895b60f7f9d0ab9421846093","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/commits/48ea9bbf9fbd9835895b60f7f9d0ab9421846093"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18365190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JReque","id":18365190,"login":"JReque","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzY1MTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/commits/250e55a0cff6e69fdd0194a8ee4bff4ed7bb6833/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T03:58:41Z","email":"jrequena9@gmail.com","name":"Jesus Requena"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T03:58:41Z","email":"jrequena9@gmail.com","name":"Jesus Requena"},"message":"fix(table): measure expanded rows so virtualization and expand coexist (F2)\n\nF1 shipped windowing with a declared `row-height` and refused to run\nalongside `expandedRowElement`, because an expanded row''s height is not\nknowable in advance: the consumer mounts arbitrary content into the\nhost. That restriction is now lifted.\n\nExpanded rows are measured with a ResizeObserver and their height is\nfolded into the row offsets:\n\n  offset(i) = i * rowHeight + sum(measured heights of expanded rows above i)\n\nThis is affordable precisely because the set of open rows is tiny by\nnature — nobody has ten thousand rows expanded at once — so the\nmeasured map stays a handful of entries while collapsed rows keep\ncosting pure arithmetic. `_indexAtOffset` inverts the same function to\nturn a scroll offset back into a row index, walking only the short list\nof expanded rows to find the linear segment the offset falls in.\n\nThe observer also fires while a row animates open, so offsets track the\ntransition instead of jumping when it ends. A height change ABOVE the\nrendered window compensates `scrollTop` by the same delta, so expanding\nan offscreen row does not yank the viewport out from under the user.\n\nRows are never recycled across keys, which is what makes this safe: an\nexpanded row scrolled out of the window leaves the DOM, but its host\nelement and cleanup stay cached against its key, so scrolling back\nreattaches the SAME host with no remount and no cleanup call. Measured\nheights are released in `_teardownKey` along with the rest of the row''s\nstate, so a collapse returns the scroll height to its baseline.\n\nWindowed cost at 10.000 rows with expand enabled: mount 3ms (was 422ms),\nsort 1.3ms (was 204ms), toggle 10ms (was 241ms), 192 nodes (was 90.019).","tree":{"sha":"d2bdc7cf77d2d09074944408e319eea7e2b263ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/git/trees/d2bdc7cf77d2d09074944408e319eea7e2b263ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/git/commits/250e55a0cff6e69fdd0194a8ee4bff4ed7bb6833","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18365190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JReque","id":18365190,"login":"JReque","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzY1MTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/JReque/reke-ui/commit/250e55a0cff6e69fdd0194a8ee4bff4ed7bb6833","node_id":"C_kwDORd369doAKDI1MGU1NWEwY2ZmNmU2OWZkZDAxOTRhOGVlNGJmZjRlZDdiYjY4MzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/JReque/reke-ui/commit/e3f2ae4a8d9ee0b36de38b9f9b34b4abaa1fd308","sha":"e3f2ae4a8d9ee0b36de38b9f9b34b4abaa1fd308","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/commits/e3f2ae4a8d9ee0b36de38b9f9b34b4abaa1fd308"}],"sha":"250e55a0cff6e69fdd0194a8ee4bff4ed7bb6833","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/commits/250e55a0cff6e69fdd0194a8ee4bff4ed7bb6833"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18365190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JReque","id":18365190,"login":"JReque","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzY1MTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/commits/e3f2ae4a8d9ee0b36de38b9f9b34b4abaa1fd308/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T03:41:02Z","email":"jrequena9@gmail.com","name":"Jesus Requena"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T03:41:02Z","email":"jrequena9@gmail.com","name":"Jesus Requena"},"message":"fix(table): add opt-in row virtualization (F1, fixed row height)\n\nRendering every row made the table unusable at corporate dataset sizes.\nMeasured on Chromium with 5 columns: mount is linear at ~44us/row, so\n5.000 rows cost 210ms to mount and 128ms per interaction, and 10.000\nrows cost 425ms and 228ms. The `guard` work landed earlier holds\n`column.render` calls per toggle at exactly 10 regardless of row count,\nbut wall time still scaled, because a table is a single layout context:\nchanging one row''s height relayouts all of them. No JS-level\noptimization can fix that — only having fewer nodes in the DOM.\n\nAdds opt-in windowing behind `virtualized`, with `row-height` and\n`max-height` declared by the consumer. Only the rows intersecting the\nviewport plus `overscan` are rendered; spacer rows carry the scroll\nheight of the rest, so the scrollbar still reports the real dataset\nsize. Row offsets are pure arithmetic from the declared `row-height`,\navailable on the first frame with no measure-then-render pass.\n\nDeliberately a prop rather than an automatic row-count threshold:\nwindowing requires a bounded-height scroll container, so enabling it\nsilently once a dataset crossed some boundary would change a consumer''s\nlayout without a code change.\n\nWindowed results at the same sizes: mount is flat at ~2.5ms and node\ncount flat at 228 from 100 rows through 10.000 (157x faster mount at\n10.000 rows, 289ms sort down to 0.9ms).\n\nRows carry their absolute dataset index, so striping, `reke-row-click`\nand key resolution are unaffected by which window is rendered. The\ntable switches to `table-layout: fixed` so column widths stop depending\non the rendered subset, exposes `aria-rowcount`/`aria-rowindex` for the\nrows that are not in the DOM, and makes the scroll container keyboard\nfocusable (caught by axe).\n\n`expandedRowElement` is not supported with `virtualized` yet and raises\na dev error: an expanded row has a height the window math cannot\npredict. Measured expand rows are F2.","tree":{"sha":"47eddcd65390734a5d02c81db8fecd646901c722","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/git/trees/47eddcd65390734a5d02c81db8fecd646901c722"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/git/commits/e3f2ae4a8d9ee0b36de38b9f9b34b4abaa1fd308","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18365190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JReque","id":18365190,"login":"JReque","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzY1MTkw","organizations_url":"ht