"d9eb3a379a005a16f99a40f5014225c03e30dd6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/commits/d9eb3a379a005a16f99a40f5014225c03e30dd6f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18365190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JReque","id":18365190,"login":"JReque","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzY1MTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/commits/1fa707509885dafbd627e39948963759aadbbc68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T20:47:17Z","email":"jrequena9@gmail.com","name":"Jesús Requena Pérez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T20:47:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Develop (#38)\n\n* fix(reke-table): expanded row spans full width and animates open/close (#33)\n\n* fix(reke-table): expanded row spans full width and animates open/close\n\nThe expand row put display:grid on the <tr>, which made the browser\nignore colspan and shrink the expand <td> to content width (~200px)\ninstead of spanning the table. Keep native table display on tr/td and\nmove the grid-rows reveal onto a dedicated .expand-grid wrapper whose\nsingle real grid item (.expand-inner) carries overflow:hidden +\nmin-height:0, so 0fr actually clips to zero.\n\nAlso add an enter animation: freshly-expanded rows render collapsed for\none frame, then release on the next rAF so the grid transition runs\n0fr -> 1fr instead of popping open. transitionend now fires on\n.expand-grid; the collapse-end listener and cleanup paths follow it.\n\nTests: align flushExpandTransition to dispatch on .expand-grid and add\nflushEnterTransition for the one-frame enter settle.\n\n* test(reke-table): use flushEnterTransition on toggleExpand open path\n\nThe open assertion waited only for updateComplete, but a freshly-expanded\nrow renders collapsed for one frame and releases on the next rAF. Under CI\ncoverage timing the collapsed class was still present, so the non-collapsed\nassertion got null. flushEnterTransition (already used elsewhere) makes it\ndeterministic.\n\n* feat(reke-combobox): searchable select component (#34)\n\n* feat(reke-combobox): add searchable select component\n\nType-to-filter select with keyboard navigation, fixed-position dropdown\nthat escapes ancestor overflow, and optional per-option images. Fully\ntokenized (colors, spacing, radius, fonts, shadows) with fallbacks.\nEmits reke-change and reke-search. Wired into barrel, React bridge, and\npackage exports. 13 tests (rendering/behavior/a11y) passing.\n\n* style(reke-combobox): apply biome formatting\n\n* docs: add npm button to landing hero and bump component count to 17 (#35)","tree":{"sha":"cd1025e8622f702f5739e5d72c24807d15dc8a35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/git/trees/cd1025e8622f702f5739e5d72c24807d15dc8a35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/git/commits/1fa707509885dafbd627e39948963759aadbbc68","verification":{"payload":"tree cd1025e8622f702f5739e5d72c24807d15dc8a35\nparent e27b05539b927d8a7f860296b9f0f14b2ccfa78f\nparent 382027276c044d57f6f4560a2d129862b97334ad\nauthor Jesús Requena Pérez <jrequena9@gmail.com> 1784407637 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784407637 -0300\n\nDevelop (#38)\n\n* fix(reke-table): expanded row spans full width and animates open/close (#33)\n\n* fix(reke-table): expanded row spans full width and animates open/close\n\nThe expand row put display:grid on the <tr>, which made the browser\nignore colspan and shrink the expand <td> to content width (~200px)\ninstead of spanning the table. Keep native table display on tr/td and\nmove the grid-rows reveal onto a dedicated .expand-grid wrapper whose\nsingle real grid item (.expand-inner) carries overflow:hidden +\nmin-height:0, so 0fr actually clips to zero.\n\nAlso add an enter animation: freshly-expanded rows render collapsed for\none frame, then release on the next rAF so the grid transition runs\n0fr -> 1fr instead of popping open. transitionend now fires on\n.expand-grid; the collapse-end listener and cleanup paths follow it.\n\nTests: align flushExpandTransition to dispatch on .expand-grid and add\nflushEnterTransition for the one-frame enter settle.\n\n* test(reke-table): use flushEnterTransition on toggleExpand open path\n\nThe open assertion waited only for updateComplete, but a freshly-expanded\nrow renders collapsed for one frame and releases on the next rAF. Under CI\ncoverage timing the collapsed class was still present, so the non-collapsed\nassertion got null. flushEnterTransition (already used elsewhere) makes it\ndeterministic.\n\n* feat(reke-combobox): searchable select component (#34)\n\n* feat(reke-combobox): add searchable select component\n\nType-to-filter select with keyboard navigation, fixed-position dropdown\nthat escapes ancestor overflow, and optional per-option images. Fully\ntokenized (colors, spacing, radius, fonts, shadows) with fallbacks.\nEmits reke-change and reke-search. Wired into barrel, React bridge, and\npackage exports. 13 tests (rendering/behavior/a11y) passing.\n\n* style(reke-combobox): apply biome formatting\n\n* docs: add npm button to landing hero and bump component count to 17 (#35)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqW+ZVCRC1aQ7uu5Uh