18365190?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JReque","id":18365190,"login":"JReque","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzY1MTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JReque","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/commits/a1351dabdeed79789747514f2fc6fb28a2b1e92f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T04:04:20Z","email":"jrequena9@gmail.com","name":"Jesús Requena Pérez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T04:04:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(reke-table): expanded row spans full width and animates open/close (#33)\n\n* fix(reke-table): expanded row spans full width and animates open/close\n\nThe expand row put display:grid on the <tr>, which made the browser\nignore colspan and shrink the expand <td> to content width (~200px)\ninstead of spanning the table. Keep native table display on tr/td and\nmove the grid-rows reveal onto a dedicated .expand-grid wrapper whose\nsingle real grid item (.expand-inner) carries overflow:hidden +\nmin-height:0, so 0fr actually clips to zero.\n\nAlso add an enter animation: freshly-expanded rows render collapsed for\none frame, then release on the next rAF so the grid transition runs\n0fr -> 1fr instead of popping open. transitionend now fires on\n.expand-grid; the collapse-end listener and cleanup paths follow it.\n\nTests: align flushExpandTransition to dispatch on .expand-grid and add\nflushEnterTransition for the one-frame enter settle.\n\n* test(reke-table): use flushEnterTransition on toggleExpand open path\n\nThe open assertion waited only for updateComplete, but a freshly-expanded\nrow renders collapsed for one frame and releases on the next rAF. Under CI\ncoverage timing the collapsed class was still present, so the non-collapsed\nassertion got null. flushEnterTransition (already used elsewhere) makes it\ndeterministic.","tree":{"sha":"85ee3e315facc01898f1ffa43656ad689bc7466c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/git/trees/85ee3e315facc01898f1ffa43656ad689bc7466c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JReque/reke-ui/git/commits/a1351dabdeed79789747514f2fc6fb28a2b1e92f","verification":{"payload":"tree 85ee3e315facc01898f1ffa43656ad689bc7466c\nparent 645a2200c5c4cbc2b54ba0791f7ed08e22d22083\nauthor Jesús Requena Pérez <jrequena9@gmail.com> 1784347460 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784347460 -0300\n\nfix(reke-table): expanded row spans full width and animates open/close (#33)\n\n* fix(reke-table): expanded row spans full width and animates open/close\n\nThe expand row put display:grid on the <tr>, which made the browser\nignore colspan and shrink the expand <td> to content width (~200px)\ninstead of spanning the table. Keep native table display on tr/td and\nmove the grid-rows reveal onto a dedicated .expand-grid wrapper whose\nsingle real grid item (.expand-inner) carries overflow:hidden +\nmin-height:0, so 0fr actually clips to zero.\n\nAlso add an enter animation: freshly-expanded rows render collapsed for\none frame, then release on the next rAF so the grid transition runs\n0fr -> 1fr instead of popping open. transitionend now fires on\n.expand-grid; the collapse-end listener and cleanup paths follow it.\n\nTests: align flushExpandTransition to dispatch on .expand-grid and add\nflushEnterTransition for the one-frame enter settle.\n\n* test(reke-table): use flushEnterTransition on toggleExpand open path\n\nThe open assertion waited only for updateComplete, but a freshly-expanded\nrow renders collapsed for one frame and releases on the next rAF. Under CI\ncoverage timing the collapsed class was still present, so the non-collapsed\nassertion got null. flushEnterTransition (already used elsewhere) makes it\ndeterministic.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWvtECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeIIQAK+KP+8Z2WXo8UQxCxKl5Hrt\nDcRgKZZTofvGVyvwMo+mACYMta5MTkzg6nZtalwhdKu6Mmic6PmWH+mdzyGt0fAi\nxIivKA5vkyX9AWUqPdJ6WphA8XaPlXa9nRzMSbkThvJkZTZmik00fbDj2LFXRvvL\nJRXWloiJ9UZkalVOw7MfTg1FzbNSaet4OIXSkQGNm5NDRrDCXiz1+Ut6owll4o/S\no34Gxokn+wALef1QjxZdNQKGjaATndR3t+ESgSGzy5xAD7c3Xx+7giEIRyiwHwr6\ngc2wrkDsRLsEHoZbsJtlHYiPiK1upPaEsl/4bmJZmhBNE3lJ6Bir+gSgU6/sfjI0\nGV/DKfVHaO34/z1PpsngkgFnf8rc7AbwiZ2QZy/U6vL+OU4xoe0GmNKXrZjkSwCL\nsmoECFpAH2xvQUQRCZESF6p1TaFis6oyLhU3YFZpZAdU4KYmQjcVOHuTdZ6x/r9c\nLnIfpuNiAHhF1mTz70HbaFtFzQicO1WJ5k+x5MIzdicbIzP6Ub9drBv9X/o3Hr6C\nog7nukqpMzGKQ7oh+70U4CwNZdXXXaknHLQBiH76XmtFBt5TNGwMQNYStATnlxqh\nrjhxTTJmStq1+2p1hYjBSvTK2+MQKBXNXe/s8CA8Qe4A+3PSc+aQNyyhJMuS9L3q\nlG8mEqAydhhlAVi8ze23\n=e5c6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-18T04:04:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/