gen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/d895987366b4d526351f31f91a591d779eb6605f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/be1526fe17da69f03e9c5622e0cf0021dcebf6f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T11:50:38Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T11:50:38Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"docs(buzz,berd): converge all surfaces on verified pilot status\n\nBoth integrations are now verified live (Buzz: doctor/post/read round-trip\nagainst a real relay + buzz binary; Berd: goosed skills list confirms live\ndiscovery of all five bridged skills). Flip both to `pilot` (built and\nverified, not yet in production) everywhere they''re described:\n\n- docs/MODULES.md + site/src/data/modules.yaml: in-dev -> pilot, status\n  prose rewritten to name what''s verified and what dogfood work remains\n- data/packages-matrix.yaml: buzz-integration dormant -> active, notes\n  rewritten to drop the now-false \"nothing runs yet\" / \"CLI_MAP is\n  guesswork\" claims\n- docs/agent-plans/{interop-plugin-architecture,QUEUE}.md: rows/entries\n  updated to reflect built+verified pilot status\n- HEARTBEAT.md: ticked the Buzz Task 1/npub/Task-8-Step-1 prerequisites\n  and the Berd live-discovery prerequisite as done, leaving the 5-session\n  tallies, skill-mirror sync, and Goose-exercise+pruning pass open\n- docs/integrations/berd.md: added a dated \"Verified 2026-08-29\" section\n  recording the goosed skills list evidence, superseding the\n  PENDING-OPERATOR marker for discovery only\n- modules/org-os-buzz/module.yaml: corrected stale \"buzz-cli\" wording\n\nGates: npm run validate:structure (53/53), site modules-catalog test\n(15/15), prettier --check on touched files (no new violations vs baseline).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1f05046276c956d4518f2e76ceb929084eed7c2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/1f05046276c956d4518f2e76ceb929084eed7c2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/be1526fe17da69f03e9c5622e0cf0021dcebf6f4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/be1526fe17da69f03e9c5622e0cf0021dcebf6f4","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKGJlMTUyNmZlMTdkYTY5ZjAzZTljNTYyMmUwY2YwMDIxZGNlYmY2ZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/5be2fb14962cf020bfa05a918e8e92a2ad47041f","sha":"5be2fb14962cf020bfa05a918e8e92a2ad47041f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/5be2fb14962cf020bfa05a918e8e92a2ad47041f"}],"sha":"be1526fe17da69f03e9c5622e0cf0021dcebf6f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/be1526fe17da69f03e9c5622e0cf0021dcebf6f4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/5be2fb14962cf020bfa05a918e8e92a2ad47041f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T11:38:59Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T11:38:59Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"docs(buzz): flip VERIFIED.md to verified and correct the surface docs\n\nRecord the 2026-08-29 Task 1 verification against a live local relay\n(deploy/compose, ghcr.io/block/buzz:main): the real buzz binary, HTTP\nrelay, BUZZ_PRIVATE_KEY, verb/flag contract, exit codes, and error\nshape. Update TOOLS.md with the real npub and channel UUID, correct the\nrelay URL scheme, and update .env.example placeholders to match.\nAppend a dated reconciliation note to the design spec recording that\nthe --tag-based provenance design was replaced by a content trailer,\nwith operator approval, rather than rewriting the original decisions.","tree":{"sha":"700dc31a0d04f583a83ab46b1952e93abf193b84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/700dc31a0d04f583a83ab46b1952e93abf193b84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/5be2fb14962cf020bfa05a918e8e92a2ad47041f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/5be2fb14962cf020bfa05a918e8e92a2ad47041f","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDViZTJmYjE0OTYyY2YwMjBiZmEwNWE5MThlOGU5MmEyYWQ0NzA0MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/39296ce3e5e7f20262f96fd34744855215f6ae5f","sha":"39296ce3e5e7f20262f96fd34744855215f6ae5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/39296ce3e5e7f20262f96fd34744855215f6ae5f"}],"sha":"5be2fb14962cf020bfa05a918e8e92a2ad47041f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/5be2fb14962cf020bfa05a918e8e92a2ad47041f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/39296ce3e5e7f20262f96fd34744855215f6ae5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T11:38:53Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T11:38:53Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"fix(buzz): reconcile wrapper against the real buzz CLI (Task 1 verified)\n\nTask 1 ran against a live local relay; nearly every documented guess in\nCLI_MAP, loadConfig, and status() was wrong. Reconcile lib/buzz.mjs and\nits scripts+tests to the verified contract: binary is `buzz` (not\nbuzz-cli), relay is HTTP (not ws://), identity env var is\nBUZZ_PRIVATE_KEY (not BUZZ_NSEC), verbs are `messages send` / `messages\nget` / `channels list` (not post/read/status), there is no --json or\n--tag flag, `messages get` returns a top-level array, and status() now\nuses the verified exit codes (2 relay-down, 3 auth) instead of guessing\nfrom a single bundled probe. Provenance moves from the nonexistent\n--tag flag to a trailer appended to the posted content, per operator\ndecision.","tree":{"sha":"0bed9f811854ec789f35326d046daefb3273a10c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/0bed9f811854ec789f35326d046daefb3273a10c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/39296ce3e5e7f20262f96fd34744855215f6ae5f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/39296ce3e5e7f20262f96fd34744855215f6ae5f","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDM5Mjk2Y2UzZTVlN2YyMDI2MmY5NmZkMzQ3NDQ4NTUyMTVmNmFlNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/cde8d6c3c8191ee65508ba6f9cc0b49d570d14ff","sha":"cde8d6c3c8191ee65508ba6f9cc0b49d570d14ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/cde8d6c3c8191ee65508ba6f9cc0b49d570d14ff"}],"sha":"39296ce3e5e7f20262f96fd34744855215f6ae5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/39296ce3e5e7f20262f96fd34744855215f6ae5f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/cde8d6c3c8191ee65508ba6f9cc0b49d570d14ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T11:11:55Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T11:11:55Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"merge: Berd module #4 + Buzz module #3 (v0.6 Actives #4/#5)\n\nTwo integrations, built and reviewed on feat/v06-integrations:\n\norg-os-berd (module #4) — formalizes the shipped agent-personas layer and\nadds scripts/sync-skills-berd.mjs, a marker-guarded mirror materializing\nfive curated skills into Berd''s project-local .agents/skills/. Drift\n--check wired into selftest.\n\norg-os-buzz (module #3) — a fail-open comms lane over the buzz-cli binary:\n/close posts a SHA-tagged session digest, /initialize reads the channel\nback. Never blocks a session.\n\nBoth catalogued in-dev and honestly unverified: no buzz-cli has run here\nand Berd''s bridge is unconfirmed in a real session. Deferred verification\nis tracked in HEARTBEAT.md.\n\n29 commits, 12 per-task reviews, 9 fix rounds, 1 final whole-branch review.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tdocs/agent-plans/QUEUE.md","tree":{"sha":"d2f6762c54593082c29a39aef07347a477eeef96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/d2f6762c54593082c29a39aef07347a477eeef96"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/cde8d6c3c8191ee65508ba6f9cc0b49d570d14ff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/cde8d6c3c8191ee65508ba6f9cc0b49d570d14ff","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKGNkZThkNmMzYzgxOTFlZTY1NTA4YmE2ZjljYzBiNDlkNTcwZDE0ZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/76596fc4341386488eebac3a7c34d61e66e5a498","sha":"76596fc4341386488eebac3a7c34d61e66e5a498","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/76596fc4341386488eebac3a7c34d61e66e5a498"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/6f0227e4b2c4620013f954144c26b3820553b4d9","sha":"6f0227e4b2c4620013f954144c26b3820553b4d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/6f0227e4b2c4620013f954144c26b3820553b4d9"}],"sha":"cde8d6c3c8191ee65508ba6f9cc0b49d570d14ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/cde8d6c3c8191ee65508ba6f9cc0b49d570d14ff"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/6f0227e4b2c4620013f954144c26b3820553b4d9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:13:57Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:13:57Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"docs(heartbeat): note in-repo skill surfaces missing buzz hooks\n\nFinal-review finding 7. The same class of gap already tracked for the\n~/.claude/skills/ post-merge sync exists in-repo too: skills/initialize/\nSKILL.md never received the read-back hook (sync-commands.mjs skips\ngenerating a command-skill for /initialize since a real skill already\nowns that name) while skills/commands/close/SKILL.md did receive the\npost hook, and skills/org-os-init/SKILL.md (one of the five skills\nbridged into Berd) carries neither hook. Net effect: close posts but\ninitialize never reads, so the tracker''s 5-consecutive-session\nacceptance can''t be satisfied from Hermes or Berd surfaces either.\nExtends the existing prerequisite bullet in place — no restructuring.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d28ad30e5d53bec1b5de1e9ec8f52ba862afe25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/1d28ad30e5d53bec1b5de1e9ec8f52ba862afe25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/6f0227e4b2c4620013f954144c26b3820553b4d9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/6f0227e4b2c4620013f954144c26b3820553b4d9","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDZmMDIyN2U0YjJjNDYyMDAxM2Y5NTQxNDRjMjZiMzgyMDU1M2I0ZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/768114fd1de2d20109683e93ce5264598e9343ed","sha":"768114fd1de2d20109683e93ce5264598e9343ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/768114fd1de2d20109683e93ce5264598e9343ed"}],"sha":"6f0227e4b2c4620013f954144c26b3820553b4d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/6f0227e4b2c4620013f954144c26b3820553b4d9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/768114fd1de2d20109683e93ce5264598e9343ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:13:51Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:13:51Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"docs(queue): reflect built in-dev status for buzz/berd modules\n\nFinal-review finding 6. QUEUE.md''s v0.6 Actives #4/#5 and interop-\nplugin-architecture.md''s Berd/Buzz matrix rows still read \"plan ready...\ngate lifted\" / \"identified + spec''d... build post-v0.5-tag\" — both\nmodules ship in this branch, so a reader landing on the queue got a\ndifferent story than one landing on docs/MODULES.md. One line each,\nnoting built + catalogued in-dev with acceptance still pending\n(HEARTBEAT.md tracker); existing spec/plan links kept, no claim that\neither lane is verified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5a11fad3432ca20fb2be74d52b9274bd2ac8a220","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/5a11fad3432ca20fb2be74d52b9274bd2ac8a220"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/768114fd1de2d20109683e93ce5264598e9343ed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/768114fd1de2d20109683e93ce5264598e9343ed","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDc2ODExNGZkMWRlMmQyMDEwOTY4M2U5M2NlNTI2NDU5OGU5MzQzZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/b3de1695e3f3d18a4d57cbd0d041d4d52e4d9be4","sha":"b3de1695e3f3d18a4d57cbd0d041d4d52e4d9be4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/b3de1695e3f3d18a4d57cbd0d041d4d52e4d9be4"}],"sha":"768114fd1de2d20109683e93ce5264598e9343ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/768114fd1de2d20109683e93ce5264598e9343ed"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/b3de1695e3f3d18a4d57cbd0d041d4d52e4d9be4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:13:44Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:13:44Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"fix(initialize): move Buzz read-back step after dashboard render\n\nFinal-review finding 4. Step 2b (Buzz channel read-back) sat before\nStep 2 (Render Dashboard) in a file that opens \"Follow these steps\nexactly\" — functionally harmless but incoherent, and it propagated\nverbatim into the .cursor/ and .opencode/ mirrors. 2b''s own content\nfeeds into Step 3''s \"Since last session\" context assembly, so it now\nsits between Step 2 and Step 3, where its name already implied it\nbelonged. Regenerated mirrors via `npm run sync:commands`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8df456cce8842b49d320803acdd09f669b645eea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/8df456cce8842b49d320803acdd09f669b645eea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/b3de1695e3f3d18a4d57cbd0d041d4d52e4d9be4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/b3de1695e3f3d18a4d57cbd0d041d4d52e4d9be4","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKGIzZGUxNjk1ZTNmM2QxOGE0ZDU3Y2JkMGQwNDFkNGQ1MmU0ZDliZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/b1f08f6d7a0478ce8625506c201bd925c52a15e4","sha":"b1f08f6d7a0478ce8625506c201bd925c52a15e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/b1f08f6d7a0478ce8625506c201bd925c52a15e4"}],"sha":"b3de1695e3f3d18a4d57cbd0d041d4d52e4d9be4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/b3de1695e3f3d18a4d57cbd0d041d4d52e4d9be4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/b1f08f6d7a0478ce8625506c201bd925c52a15e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:13:38Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:13:38Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"docs(berd): correct built status and Goose release date\n\nFinal-review finding 3. \"The bridge\" section still said module #4\norg-os-berd was \"not yet built\" — it was built in Tasks 1-4 of this\nbranch, and docs/MODULES.md''s own entry links this page as \"discovery &\nverification,\" so a cold reader following that link was told the thing\nthey just read about doesn''t exist. Now states it''s built and catalogued\nin-dev, with Goose verification (not the build) as the open item, cross-\nreferencing docs/MODULES.md''s org-os-berd entry.\n\nAlso fixed the Goose v1.25.0 date (2026-02-23 -> 2026-02-18, the actual\nrelease/commit date).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c6f7794bdd0ef8b7ef6fb382da6a86e54d0b82cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/c6f7794bdd0ef8b7ef6fb382da6a86e54d0b82cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/b1f08f6d7a0478ce8625506c201bd925c52a15e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/b1f08f6d7a0478ce8625506c201bd925c52a15e4","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKGIxZjA4ZjZkN2EwNDc4Y2U4NjI1NTA2YzIwMWJkOTI1YzUyYTE1ZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/350f12f0b2f5fe16836e73fc3368073c713e1860","sha":"350f12f0b2f5fe16836e73fc3368073c713e1860","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/350f12f0b2f5fe16836e73fc3368073c713e1860"}],"sha":"b1f08f6d7a0478ce8625506c201bd925c52a15e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/b1f08f6d7a0478ce8625506c201bd925c52a15e4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/350f12f0b2f5fe16836e73fc3368073c713e1860/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:13:32Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:13:32Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"fix(buzz): truthful doctor checks + pin CLI_MAP argv shape in tests\n\nFinal-review findings 2/5. status() early-returned all four checks as\nfalse when buzz-cli was missing, so `npm run buzz:doctor` showed \"agent\nkey\" and \"channel\" as failing even when BUZZ_NSEC/BUZZ_CHANNEL were\npopulated — both are locally knowable from cfg alone and don''t need the\nCLI. key/channel are now computed before the bin early-return; bin and\nrelay still correctly stay false without a binary.\n\nSeparately, mutation testing on the full suite found 7/10 mutations\ncaught but all three survivors were CLI_MAP constants (post→publish,\n--channel→-c everywhere, --json dropped from post argv) — every existing\ntest only asserted values, never verb/flag shape. Added three tests\npinning the exact verb + flag names for post/read/status. CLI_MAP itself\nis untouched; these pin the current unverified guesses so the eventual\nreconciliation against a real buzz-cli (VERIFIED.md step 5) is\nred-test-driven instead of a manual diff.\n\nRED/GREEN evidence and manual mutation-survivor verification in\n.superpowers/sdd/2026-08-29-buzz-integration/final-fix-wave-report.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"746acebedf150423c5fae181100fc07b633d4af0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/746acebedf150423c5fae181100fc07b633d4af0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/350f12f0b2f5fe16836e73fc3368073c713e1860","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/350f12f0b2f5fe16836e73fc3368073c713e1860","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDM1MGYxMmYwYjJmNWZlMTY4MzZlNzNmYzMzNjgwNzNjNzEzZTE4NjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/aff19ba68a98e9a7bc1ea50ee6a4f0ab79dd339f","sha":"aff19ba68a98e9a7bc1ea50ee6a4f0ab79dd339f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/aff19ba68a98e9a7bc1ea50ee6a4f0ab79dd339f"}],"sha":"350f12f0b2f5fe16836e73fc3368073c713e1860","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/350f12f0b2f5fe16836e73fc3368073c713e1860"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/aff19ba68a98e9a7bc1ea50ee6a4f0ab79dd339f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:13:23Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:13:23Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"fix(berd): guard two unhandled reads in sync-skills-berd.mjs\n\nFinal-review findings 1a/1b. A missing modules/org-os-berd/module.yaml\n(any downstream instance whose overlay covers scripts/ + templates/ but\nnot modules/) threw an uncaught ENOENT and killed the process; since the\nscript file itself is present, selftest''s optional \"berd skills mirror in\nsync\" check couldn''t SKIP it and recorded a hard FAIL on every instance\nthat simply doesn''t have the module. Now it prints a skip line and exits\n0. Separately, a target SKILL.md with malformed frontmatter threw an\nuncaught YAMLException that aborted the whole materialization loop,\nskipping every remaining skill behind it — now a per-skill hard error\n(failures++, continue), matching the existing \"not a directory\" and \"no\nfrontmatter fence\" hard-error handling.\n\nBoth regressions reproduced as failing tests before the fix (RED\ncaptured in .superpowers/sdd/2026-08-29-buzz-integration/\nfinal-fix-wave-report.md), green after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6be83b8c1fd6c101cb453c6cdd45341c2ec2c108","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/6be83b8c1fd6c101cb453c6cdd45341c2ec2c108"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/aff19ba68a98e9a7bc1ea50ee6a4f0ab79dd339f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/aff19ba68a98e9a7bc1ea50ee6a4f0ab79dd339f","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKGFmZjE5YmE2OGE5OGU5YTdiYzFlYTUwZWU2YTRmMGFiNzlkZDMzOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/3ba938174f52310fc70cf35819c76ec45c83c818","sha":"3ba938174f52310fc70cf35819c76ec45c83c818","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/3ba938174f52310fc70cf35819c76ec45c83c818"}],"sha":"aff19ba68a98e9a7bc1ea50ee6a4f0ab79dd339f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/aff19ba68a98e9a7bc1ea50ee6a4f0ab79dd339f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/3ba938174f52310fc70cf35819c76ec45c83c818/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T05:35:33Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T05:35:33Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"fix(buzz): dormant lifecycle_status; arm the dogfood acceptance tracker\n\nController ruling, on reviewer evidence: quilt-view.mjs routes\nin_framework && lifecycle_status === \"active\" into the prominent\n\"patches\" tier, and paperclip-agents-app is already dormant despite a\nreal instances_using entry — the field tracks \"is anything actually\nhappening\", not adoption. Every buzz:doctor check is currently ✗ and\nboth hooks always print a skip line, so buzz-integration is present but\ninert, like koi-bridge — dormant, not active. Notes reworded to say so\nwithout losing any of the existing detail.\n\nAdds the Buzz lane dogfood acceptance tracker to HEARTBEAT.md, mirroring\nthe Berd tracker''s pattern: deferred prerequisites named explicitly above\nthe five-session count (plan Task 1 pin-and-verify, recording the npub,\nTask 8 Step 1''s live round-trip, and syncing the machine-local skill\nmirror after this branch merges — none of them attempted here, per the\nopen Task 1 blockers and the out-of-scope ruling on ~/.claude/).","tree":{"sha":"90933c442ee1a2304ddda763836428b5d6ddd3db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/90933c442ee1a2304ddda763836428b5d6ddd3db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/3ba938174f52310fc70cf35819c76ec45c83c818","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/3ba938174f52310fc70cf35819c76ec45c83c818","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDNiYTkzODE3NGY1MjMxMGZjNzBjZjM1ODE5Yzc2ZWM0NWM4M2M4MTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/4315cf1f3542da9034a4bf2c44463f3c43c53d68","sha":"4315cf1f3542da9034a4bf2c44463f3c43c53d68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/4315cf1f3542da9034a4bf2c44463f3c43c53d68"}],"sha":"3ba938174f52310fc70cf35819c76ec45c83c818","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/3ba938174f52310fc70cf35819c76ec45c83c818"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/4315cf1f3542da9034a4bf2c44463f3c43c53d68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T05:19:56Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T05:19:56Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"feat(buzz): fail-open session hooks in initialize/close\n\nAdds two optional, fail-open touchpoints to the canonical command files:\nStep 2b in /initialize reads the Buzz channel back into session context\nwhen `buzz:doctor` is green; Step 8b in /close posts the session digest\nafter the close commit exists. The close hook writes the digest to a temp\nfile and posts with `--file` rather than a bare pipe or here-string, so\nthe invocation never depends on stdin closing on its own.\n\n`npm run sync:commands` propagates both to .opencode/, .cursor/, and the\nHermes command-skill at skills/commands/close/ (skills/commands/initialize/\nis skipped by the generator — a real `initialize` skill already owns that\nname). The generator also swept a stale `.opencode/command/` (singular)\nlegacy dir left over from before its migration-cleanup logic existed.\n\nVerified fail-open with no relay configured: `buzz:doctor` exits 2 with a\nwarn line, `buzz:read` exits 0 with a skip line, `buzz:post --file` exits 0\nwith a skip line — nothing blocks a close.","tree":{"sha":"0244257f83a9754504b35cc2e5b623c348bda23c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/0244257f83a9754504b35cc2e5b623c348bda23c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/4315cf1f3542da9034a4bf2c44463f3c43c53d68","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/4315cf1f3542da9034a4bf2c44463f3c43c53d68","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDQzMTVjZjFmMzU0MmRhOTAzNGE0YmYyYzQ0NDYzZjNjNDNjNTNkNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/cc242d91d834651a4c2e3a24fbb1ab7ea57ebc10","sha":"cc242d91d834651a4c2e3a24fbb1ab7ea57ebc10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/cc242d91d834651a4c2e3a24fbb1ab7ea57ebc10"}],"sha":"4315cf1f3542da9034a4bf2c44463f3c43c53d68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/4315cf1f3542da9034a4bf2c44463f3c43c53d68"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/cc242d91d834651a4c2e3a24fbb1ab7ea57ebc10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T05:19:39Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T05:19:39Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"feat(buzz): register org-os-buzz as module #3 (in-dev)\n\nAdds the manifest, the docs/MODULES.md + site/src/data/modules.yaml\ndouble-entry (status in-dev, honest about the unverified CLI surface and\npending npub), the TOOLS.md Buzz section, and a packages-matrix.yaml entry\nper controller ruling 11 (comparable packages already register there and\nmain''s incoming interfaces-consolidation work reads this matrix).\n\nNo live relay has been verified against; CLI_MAP in lib/buzz.mjs remains\nunverified documented defaults until the operator runs Task 1.","tree":{"sha":"8135720ce961401f13304abf0693632fb445f7c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/8135720ce961401f13304abf0693632fb445f7c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/cc242d91d834651a4c2e3a24fbb1ab7ea57ebc10","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/cc242d91d834651a4c2e3a24fbb1ab7ea57ebc10","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKGNjMjQyZDkxZDgzNDY1MWE0YzJlM2EyNGZiYjFhYjdlYTU3ZWJjMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/d63c25903e5fdc7bc5b2f9dd5044da6fe3c146eb","sha":"d63c25903e5fdc7bc5b2f9dd5044da6fe3c146eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/d63c25903e5fdc7bc5b2f9dd5044da6fe3c146eb"}],"sha":"cc242d91d834651a4c2e3a24fbb1ab7ea57ebc10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/cc242d91d834651a4c2e3a24fbb1ab7ea57ebc10"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/d63c25903e5fdc7bc5b2f9dd5044da6fe3c146eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T05:04:03Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T05:04:03Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"fix(buzz): tag truncated posts, bound git lookup, close NEW-B''s gap\n\nRound 4: three small items closing out the truncation-handling work.\n\n- item 1: a truncated post is now tagged truncated=true on the event\n  itself, not just noted in the console line. Rationale (the spec''s\n  own claim at docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-28-buzz-integration-design.md:71):\n  the Buzz log is \"a cryptographically signed mirror of session\n  history\" - a partial digest indistinguishable from a complete one in\n  that permanent log misrepresents exactly that guarantee, the same\n  class of provenance-lying-by-omission bug as the earlier wrong-repo-\n  SHA fix (M3). The console line doesn''t survive the session; the\n  event does.\n- item 2: NEW-2b (the clean-EOF-path test) never asserted the negative\n  half of NEW-B - that a complete post must NOT be flagged as\n  truncated. Structurally identical to NEW-C one round ago: positive\n  half pinned, negative half not, verified via the reviewer''s own\n  named mutation (flagging the \"end\" handler as truncated leaves all\n  other 53 tests green). No implementation change - the end handler\n  was already correct. Also tightened NEW-B''s own assertion from\n  /truncat/i to /content may be truncated/i, closing the exact class\n  of fixture-naming coupling that produced round 3''s false positive.\n- item 3: the git rev-parse execSync call had no timeout of its own,\n  so the NEW-A comment''s \"nothing blocks more than 15s\" was false -\n  the stdin read, git lookup, and CLI invoke are sequential and\n  additive, worst case ~35s with an unbounded middle term. Added a\n  5000ms timeout (falls back to sha=unknown via the existing catch,\n  same as any other git failure) and corrected the comment to state\n  the real worst case instead of a false single-stage one.\n\nRED captured first for item 3 (a hanging git shim, bounded with an\nexplicit outer kill) against unmodified HEAD; item 2 confirmed GREEN\nagainst HEAD first (no live bug) then RED against the reviewer''s named\nmutation. All 56 tests in tests/buzz-integration/ pass (up from 53).\nFull RED/GREEN evidence and an explicit \"failure modes introduced by\nthis round\" accounting - including the real trade-off that a merely-\nslow (not hung) git now gets permanently recorded as sha=unknown -\nappended to .superpowers/sdd/2026-08-29-buzz-integration/task-3-5-report.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1220db884d5729f4eefbde8447c7ca3eec7bbad1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/1220db884d5729f4eefbde8447c7ca3eec7bbad1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/d63c25903e5fdc7bc5b2f9dd5044da6fe3c146eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/d63c25903e5fdc7bc5b2f9dd5044da6fe3c146eb","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKGQ2M2MyNTkwM2U1ZmRjN2JjNWIyZjlkZDUwNDRkYTZmZTNjMTQ2ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/093e2ea3000ab2633297e45b909c88e1916ef291","sha":"093e2ea3000ab2633297e45b909c88e1916ef291","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/093e2ea3000ab2633297e45b909c88e1916ef291"}],"sha":"d63c25903e5fdc7bc5b2f9dd5044da6fe3c146eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/d63c25903e5fdc7bc5b2f9dd5044da6fe3c146eb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/093e2ea3000ab2633297e45b909c88e1916ef291/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T04:44:21Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T04:44:21Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"fix(buzz): bound the idle timer and flag timer-truncated posts\n\nThird review round named a pattern: each of the last two rounds'' fixes\ncorrectly closed the failure it targeted and opened a quieter one next\nto it (C1''s crash-guard -> silent message loss; I1''s hang-guard ->\ncontent discard; NEW-2''s content-loss fix -> unbounded read). This\nround closes the three concrete findings and treats that pattern as\nthe thing to guard against going forward.\n\n- NEW-A: readStdin()''s idle timer alone had no upper bound - a\n  producer that never goes idle (one byte every second, forever) could\n  keep re-arming it indefinitely, turning the I1 hang guard back into\n  a hang. Added a second, never-rearmed total-deadline timer\n  (default 15000ms, matching lib/buzz.mjs''s own CLI invoke() timeout)\n  alongside the idle one; whichever fires first ends the read.\n- NEW-B: a timer firing with data already buffered means the read\n  ended before natural EOF - the content may or may not be everything\n  the producer intended. Posting it is correct; announcing it as a\n  plain, unqualified success is not. The success message now says so\n  (\"stdin read stopped before EOF; content may be truncated\") only on\n  the timer path, never on the normal EOF path. Caught and fixed a\n  wording inaccuracy in my own first draft (\"stdin went idle\", which is\n  false when the total-not-idle timer is what actually fired) during\n  self-review, before it shipped.\n- NEW-C: added a test proving a genuinely empty {events: []} reply\n  still advances read-since.mjs''s marker - the implementation was\n  already correct (confirmed: this test passes against unmodified\n  HEAD), so this closes a pure test-coverage gap, verified by\n  reproducing the review''s own named mutation and confirming only this\n  new test catches it. No implementation change.\n\nRED captured first for NEW-A (bounded with an explicit 6s harness kill,\nnot reliant on the script exiting) and NEW-B against unmodified HEAD.\nAll 53 tests in tests/buzz-integration/ pass (up from 50). Full\nRED/GREEN evidence, and an explicit \"failure modes introduced by this\nround\" accounting, appended to\n.superpowers/sdd/2026-08-29-buzz-integration/task-3-5-report.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2af3ea25de2c6586c4034dcf43cfcc9a67eb1f91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/2af3ea25de2c6586c4034dcf43cfcc9a67eb1f91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/093e2ea3000ab2633297e45b909c88e1916ef291","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/093e2ea3000ab2633297e45b909c88e1916ef291","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDA5M2UyZWEzMDAwYWIyNjMzMjk3ZTQ1YjkwOWM4OGUxOTE2ZWYyOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/7f226052dd639fd0628939cac4964de3a36b0567","sha":"7f226052dd639fd0628939cac4964de3a36b0567","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/7f226052dd639fd0628939cac4964de3a36b0567"}],"sha":"093e2ea3000ab2633297e45b909c88e1916ef291","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/093e2ea3000ab2633297e45b909c88e1916ef291"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/7f226052dd639fd0628939cac4964de3a36b0567/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T04:21:34Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T04:21:34Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"fix(buzz): stop the C1/I1 fixes from losing messages and digest content\n\nRe-review of 9beba6d confirmed all nine prior findings addressed, but\nfound the fixes themselves introduced two new loss paths, plus two\ncheap items:\n\n- NEW-1: read-since.mjs''s C1 guard (Array.isArray(r.events) ? r.events\n  : []) conflated \"reply has no recognizable events array\" (a field\n  rename from buzz-cli preview drift, or `{}` from a relay proxy) with\n  \"genuinely zero new events\" — both printed \"no new messages\" and\n  fell through to the unconditional marker advance, permanently\n  skipping real messages. Worse than the crash it replaced. Now an\n  unrecognized shape gets its own loud, distinct skip line and never\n  advances the marker.\n- NEW-2: post-digest.mjs''s I1 stdin-hang fix used a one-shot total\n  timeout, so a producer that wrote the complete digest and then held\n  the pipe open (or streamed slowly but completely) had its fully- or\n  partially-buffered content discarded outright. Timer is now an idle\n  timer, reset on every chunk, and resolves with whatever has been\n  buffered rather than throwing it away — a genuinely empty read is\n  still the only case that reports a real timeout.\n- cheap: read-since.mjs''s content fallback stringified the whole event\n  (String(e)) instead of just the content field when content wasn''t a\n  string, rendering \"[object Object]\" and losing the event entirely\n  rather than just the nested payload.\n- cheap: buzz-post-digest.test.mjs computed its expected sha via a\n  top-level execSync with no guard, so a git-less checkout failed the\n  whole file to load instead of skipping the two tests that need it.\n\nBoth NEW-1 and NEW-2 covering tests were written first and confirmed\ngenuinely red against 9beba6d before the fix. All 50 tests in\ntests/buzz-integration/ pass (up from 45); full RED/GREEN evidence per\nfinding appended to\n.superpowers/sdd/2026-08-29-buzz-integration/task-3-5-report.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f4d504a6a2d8626a959c9b3485558d5405681eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/9f4d504a6a2d8626a959c9b3485558d5405681eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/7f226052dd639fd0628939cac4964de3a36b0567","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/7f226052dd639fd0628939cac4964de3a36b0567","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDdmMjI2MDUyZGQ2MzlmZDA2Mjg5MzljYWM0OTY0ZGUzYTM2YjA1Njc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/9beba6dab1569edcb06ef02cc59d64281b5ad1eb","sha":"9beba6dab1569edcb06ef02cc59d64281b5ad1eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/9beba6dab1569edcb06ef02cc59d64281b5ad1eb"}],"sha":"7f226052dd639fd0628939cac4964de3a36b0567","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/7f226052dd639fd0628939cac4964de3a36b0567"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/9beba6dab1569edcb06ef02cc59d64281b5ad1eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:59:16Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:59:16Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"fix(buzz): close crash and hang gaps found in batch review\n\nBatch review of read-since/post-digest/doctor (686e4c0) found 2 Critical\nand 4 Important defects, plus 3 minors, all reproduced with a covering\ntest written and confirmed RED first:\n\n- C1: read-since.mjs crashed (exit 1) on any reply whose `events` field\n  wasn''t a well-formed array, or whose entries weren''t well-formed\n  objects (field rename, `{}` reply, null/non-object entries). Now\n  guarded with Array.isArray + per-field validation.\n- C2: read-since.mjs crashed (exit 1) on an unwritable --state path\n  (missing parent dir, or a directory) after already printing events.\n  Now wrapped in try/catch with a skip line. Removed the now-dead\n  existsSync import that was this guard''s missing half.\n- I1: post-digest.mjs''s readFileSync(0) blocked forever on a stdin that\n  never sends EOF (open TTY/FIFO) — a silent hang, worse than any\n  fail-open exit. Replaced with an async, timeout-bounded stdin read\n  (BUZZ_STDIN_TIMEOUT_MS, default 3000ms).\n- I2: added regression tests for marker-advancement (must not advance\n  on a failed read, --since fallback must be now-24h and must actually\n  be sent) — the implementation was already correct, this closes a\n  pure test-coverage gap confirmed via mutation testing.\n- I3: lib/buzz.mjs''s status() probed `buzz-cli --version` with no\n  timeout, unlike invoke()''s 15s — doctor.mjs could hang indefinitely\n  against a wedged binary. Added timeout: 5000.\n- I4: post-digest.mjs misreported a bad --file (missing, a directory,\n  or given with no value) as \"empty digest\", hiding the real failure.\n  Now reports a distinct read/usage error.\n- M2/M3 (M3 re-weighted Important): post-digest.mjs let git''s stderr\n  leak into the /close transcript, and derived its sha tag from the\n  caller''s cwd instead of its own repo root (wrong sha when invoked\n  from elsewhere, e.g. the enclosing vault). Fixed with stdio\n  suppression and a ROOT-based cwd, matching read-since.mjs''s pattern.\n- M6: tightened a loose `sha=` prefix assertion to the exact real HEAD\n  sha, so a hardcoded fake value can''t pass.\n\nAll 19 Task 2 tests and the 11 prior Task 3-5 tests remain green; 20 new\ntests added (45 total in tests/buzz-integration/). Full RED/GREEN\nevidence per finding appended to\n.superpowers/sdd/2026-08-29-buzz-integration/task-3-5-report.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cffb4d79df6f2f038defb7852fa770004e7add7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/cffb4d79df6f2f038defb7852fa770004e7add7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/9beba6dab1569edcb06ef02cc59d64281b5ad1eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/9beba6dab1569edcb06ef02cc59d64281b5ad1eb","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDliZWJhNmRhYjE1NjllZGNiMDZlZjAyY2M1OWQ2NDI4MWI1YWQxZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/686e4c0a1c984dcc760651cc6f7c0d34e0bb8e44","sha":"686e4c0a1c984dcc760651cc6f7c0d34e0bb8e44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/686e4c0a1c984dcc760651cc6f7c0d34e0bb8e44"}],"sha":"9beba6dab1569edcb06ef02cc59d64281b5ad1eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/9beba6dab1569edcb06ef02cc59d64281b5ad1eb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/686e4c0a1c984dcc760651cc6f7c0d34e0bb8e44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:35:32Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:35:32Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"feat(buzz): doctor + npm scripts + env surface\n\nAdds packages/buzz-integration/scripts/doctor.mjs (status/loadConfig\nover lib/buzz.mjs: prints bin/relay/key/channel checks, exits 0 green\nor 2 not-ready — matching selftest warn semantics, never 1). Wires\nbuzz:doctor/buzz:post/buzz:read into root package.json and extends\n.env.example with the Buzz block plus a note that any \"#\"-bearing\nvalue must be quoted, since the .env parser treats an unquoted \"#\" as\na comment marker.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ca99c3f0c6fd0e650cc1d98b6686a27dae266209","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/ca99c3f0c6fd0e650cc1d98b6686a27dae266209"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/686e4c0a1c984dcc760651cc6f7c0d34e0bb8e44","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/686e4c0a1c984dcc760651cc6f7c0d34e0bb8e44","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDY4NmU0YzBhMWM5ODRkY2M3NjA2NTFjYzZmN2MwZDM0ZTBiYjhlNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/65a413e82a0f9620a7c6aa95baae23d0e2c286dd","sha":"65a413e82a0f9620a7c6aa95baae23d0e2c286dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/65a413e82a0f9620a7c6aa95baae23d0e2c286dd"}],"sha":"686e4c0a1c984dcc760651cc6f7c0d34e0bb8e44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/686e4c0a1c984dcc760651cc6f7c0d34e0bb8e44"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/65a413e82a0f9620a7c6aa95baae23d0e2c286dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:35:25Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:35:25Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"feat(buzz): post-digest with SHA tag, fail-open\n\nAdds packages/buzz-integration/scripts/post-digest.mjs, a thin CLI\nover lib/buzz.mjs''s postEvent/loadConfig: reads a session digest from\n--file or stdin, tags it sha=<git HEAD> + source=org-os-session, and\nalways exits 0 so a Buzz outage can never block /close.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a1f108ce8cf9317797a0022d0b4db622a0bd6ae9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/a1f108ce8cf9317797a0022d0b4db622a0bd6ae9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/65a413e82a0f9620a7c6aa95baae23d0e2c286dd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/65a413e82a0f9620a7c6aa95baae23d0e2c286dd","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDY1YTQxM2U4MmEwZjk2MjBhN2M2YWE5NWJhYWUyM2QwZTJjMjg2ZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/e2de7b6c4e0fc982e7a3b61a2582b77d755b697b","sha":"e2de7b6c4e0fc982e7a3b61a2582b77d755b697b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/e2de7b6c4e0fc982e7a3b61a2582b77d755b697b"}],"sha":"65a413e82a0f9620a7c6aa95baae23d0e2c286dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/65a413e82a0f9620a7c6aa95baae23d0e2c286dd"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/e2de7b6c4e0fc982e7a3b61a2582b77d755b697b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:35:20Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:35:20Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"feat(buzz): read-since with fail-open marker window\n\nAdds packages/buzz-integration/scripts/read-since.mjs, a thin CLI over\nlib/buzz.mjs''s readChannel/loadConfig: prints new channel events since\nthe last recorded marker (or a 24h fallback window), always exits 0,\nand never lets a relay/CLI failure block a session.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"08274863503602d31ad892a910bce1f2f9ab5530","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/08274863503602d31ad892a910bce1f2f9ab5530"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/e2de7b6c4e0fc982e7a3b61a2582b77d755b697b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/e2de7b6c4e0fc982e7a3b61a2582b77d755b697b","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKGUyZGU3YjZjNGUwZmM5ODJlN2EzYjYxYTI1ODJiNzdkNzU1YjY5N2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/e89e65c321903aa3e17e4647ee5f7cbe9b631ef3","sha":"e89e65c321903aa3e17e4647ee5f7cbe9b631ef3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/e89e65c321903aa3e17e4647ee5f7cbe9b631ef3"}],"sha":"e2de7b6c4e0fc982e7a3b61a2582b77d755b697b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/e2de7b6c4e0fc982e7a3b61a2582b77d755b697b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/e89e65c321903aa3e17e4647ee5f7cbe9b631ef3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:22:45Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:22:45Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"style(buzz): prettier format + fix remaining .env comment/quote edge cases\n\nPrettier --write on both files: confirmed via a scratch comparison (CLI_MAP\nextracted before/after into isolated modules, called with representative\npost/read/status args) that every argv array element is byte-identical —\nonly line breaks changed, so this does not violate the CLI_MAP\nbyte-identical requirement (which governs the argv reaching buzz-cli, not\nsource whitespace).\n\nAlso closes the two .env parsing edge cases flagged but deferred in the\nprior fix round:\n- `KEY=value# note` (comment with no preceding space) now strips the\n  comment, matching real dotenv semantics (any unquoted \"#\" starts a\n  comment, whitespace or not).\n- `KEY=\"value\" # note` (quoted value plus trailing comment) now strips\n  both the surrounding quotes and the trailing comment.\n\nparseEnvValue rewritten from regex-based to indexOf-based: quoted values\ntake everything up to the matching closing quote (discarding whatever\nfollows, comment or not); unquoted values are cut at the first \"#\"\nregardless of preceding whitespace. Two new tests added, confirmed RED\nagainst the pre-fix parser before the change, GREEN after.","tree":{"sha":"24de1f74d2d3a4c5509950ff9b4bb49c97dfbf27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/24de1f74d2d3a4c5509950ff9b4bb49c97dfbf27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/e89e65c321903aa3e17e4647ee5f7cbe9b631ef3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/e89e65c321903aa3e17e4647ee5f7cbe9b631ef3","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKGU4OWU2NWMzMjE5MDNhYTNlMTdlNDY0N2VlNWY3Y2JlOWI2MzFlZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/cc48f28166f58e91c52512fad83c298c0f9ed114","sha":"cc48f28166f58e91c52512fad83c298c0f9ed114","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/cc48f28166f58e91c52512fad83c298c0f9ed114"}],"sha":"e89e65c321903aa3e17e4647ee5f7cbe9b631ef3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/e89e65c321903aa3e17e4647ee5f7cbe9b631ef3"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/cc48f28166f58e91c52512fad83c298c0f9ed114/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:16:43Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:16:43Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"fix(buzz): loadConfig fail-open, robust .env parsing, fail-open test coverage\n\nReview of 0eb9030 found a Critical spec violation and three Important gaps\nin the buzz-cli wrapper (CLI_MAP itself untouched, per Ruling 2):\n\n- CRITICAL: postEvent/readChannel/status called `cfg ?? loadConfig()`\n  outside their guarding try, so any loadConfig() failure (.env unreadable\n  as a directory -> EISDIR, or permission-denied -> EACCES) propagated as\n  an uncaught exception, violating the spec''s \"never throw\" contract that\n  /close depends on. Fixed by making loadConfig itself total (its file\n  read is now wrapped in try/catch, falling back to safe defaults on any\n  read failure) and by moving cfg resolution inside invoke()''s and\n  status()''s try blocks as defense in depth.\n\n- Important 1: .env parsing only recognized bare `KEY=value` lines.\n  Quoted values kept their literal quotes, trailing \" # comment\" text\n  folded into the value, `export KEY=value` didn''t match at all, and any\n  CRLF line ending made the whole line silently fail to match (reverting\n  to defaults). Replaced the single regex with parseEnvFile/parseEnvValue\n  that strips a trailing \\r, skips blank/comment lines, accepts an\n  optional `export ` prefix, strips a matching pair of surrounding quotes\n  (leaving \"#\" inside untouched), and otherwise strips a trailing comment.\n\n- Important 2: fail-open was only asserted for status() with a\n  nonexistent binary. Added coverage for postEvent/readChannel against a\n  non-zero-exit CLI, non-JSON stdout, and empty stdout, plus the\n  loadConfig-level EISDIR/EACCES cases above.\n\n- Important 3: the \"passes since and returns events\" test never inspected\n  argv.json, so the \"passes since\" half was unverified. Now asserts\n  --since and its value reach the CLI argv.\n\n- Minor: postEvent() now rejects a missing `content` locally (ok:false)\n  instead of silently invoking the CLI with a stripped/undefined argv\n  element.\n\nTests written first against 0eb9030 and confirmed to fail for the\ndescribed reasons before the fix (see task-2-report.md addendum).","tree":{"sha":"6df6768002c7cbe07902b278dfb959ddfbf4dae7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/6df6768002c7cbe07902b278dfb959ddfbf4dae7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/cc48f28166f58e91c52512fad83c298c0f9ed114","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/cc48f28166f58e91c52512fad83c298c0f9ed114","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKGNjNDhmMjgxNjZmNThlOTFjNTI1MTJmYWQ4M2MyOThjMGY5ZWQxMTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/0eb90309d48a2b2b73bdb68b3de26e7d465f4800","sha":"0eb90309d48a2b2b73bdb68b3de26e7d465f4800","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/0eb90309d48a2b2b73bdb68b3de26e7d465f4800"}],"sha":"cc48f28166f58e91c52512fad83c298c0f9ed114","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/cc48f28166f58e91c52512fad83c298c0f9ed114"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/0eb90309d48a2b2b73bdb68b3de26e7d465f4800/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:01:41Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T03:01:41Z","email":"opencode@local","name":"OpenCode"},"message":"feat(buzz): wrapper lib over pinned buzz-cli (TDD)\n\nCLI_MAP encodes unverified documented defaults from the buzz-integration\nplan (Task 1''s real verification is deferred to the operator — Docker,\njust, hermit, buzz-cli, goose all absent from this environment). VERIFIED.md\nlands as an explicit PENDING stub with a table skeleton for the operator to\nfill in once they clone+pin block/buzz and exercise buzz-cli for real.\n\nTests use a fixture fake buzz-cli (node script, no real binary/relay).","tree":{"sha":"14ecf18b436cd626b2dcf03101f7a88c04e4026a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/trees/14ecf18b436cd626b2dcf03101f7a88c04e4026a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/git/commits/0eb90309d48a2b2b73bdb68b3de26e7d465f4800","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/0eb90309d48a2b2b73bdb68b3de26e7d465f4800","node_id":"C_kwDOReKBZtoAKDBlYjkwMzA5ZDQ4YTJiMmI3M2JkYjY4YjNkZTI2ZTdkNDY1ZjQ4MDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commit/569ac04940791ca931f3ad22d25b8d0d03ce2e63","sha":"569ac04940791ca931f3ad22d25b8d0d03ce2e63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/569ac04940791ca931f3ad22d25b8d0d03ce2e63"}],"sha":"0eb90309d48a2b2b73bdb68b3de26e7d465f4800","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/regen-coordination/org-os-template/commits/0eb90309d48a2b2b73bdb6