n/commit/b78feac448b71301481e54b60b93f6ad169d36a4","sha":"b78feac448b71301481e54b60b93f6ad169d36a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel-plugin/commits/b78feac448b71301481e54b60b93f6ad169d36a4"}],"sha":"26a8fbe396ba6740b8df71c16973707d88709370","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel-plugin/commits/26a8fbe396ba6740b8df71c16973707d88709370"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41597851?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oulay2002/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oulay2002/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oulay2002/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oulay2002/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oulay2002","id":41597851,"login":"oulay2002","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNTk3ODUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oulay2002/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oulay2002/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oulay2002/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oulay2002/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oulay2002/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oulay2002","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel-plugin/commits/b78feac448b71301481e54b60b93f6ad169d36a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T21:26:51Z","email":"41597851+oulay2002@users.noreply.github.com","name":"oulay2002"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T21:26:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[hooks] Detect the Vercel CLI on Windows (#143)\n\n* [hooks] Detect the Vercel CLI on Windows\n\nThe session-start profiler tells every Windows user to install a CLI they\nalready have. Two independent defects, both in the resolve-then-spawn path:\n\n1. `getBinaryPathCandidates` put the bare name ahead of every PATHEXT\n   suffix. npm lays down three entries per global binary in %APPDATA%\\npm:\n   `vercel` (a POSIX sh shim), `vercel.CMD` and `vercel.ps1`. The bare shim\n   won, and spawnSync rejects it with ENOENT.\n\n2. Even once `vercel.CMD` is selected, execFileSync cannot run it. Since the\n   fix for CVE-2024-27980, Node refuses .cmd/.bat without `shell: true`\n   (EINVAL). This hit the `npm view vercel version` probe too, so the\n   outdated-version branch was dead code on Windows.\n\nObserved on Windows 11, Node 24.18.0, with Vercel CLI 58.9.0 on PATH:\n\n    (no extension)  execFileSync -> ENOENT\n    .CMD            execFileSync -> EINVAL\n    .ps1            execFileSync -> EFTYPE\n\nOrder candidates by what Node can actually spawn (.EXE/.COM/.CMD/.BAT\nfirst, remaining PATHEXT entries next, bare name last), and route batch\nwrappers through the shell with the path quoted, since cmd.exe re-parses\nthe command line and would split an unquoted path on its spaces.\n\nAlso stop reporting `installed: false` when the binary resolved but the\nversion probe failed - the CLI is on PATH, and advising a reinstall is\nthe one answer that cannot help.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Run Windows batch wrappers from one quoted command string\n\nshell: true with an args array triggers Node 24''s DEP0190 warning on\nevery session start. Build a single command with the path quoted and\nrun it with execSync instead.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: molebox <rich@vercel.com>","tree":{"sha":"e8ea7028f17ecd889074d344713e0fa3ac20ac11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel-plugin/git/trees/e8ea7028f17ecd889074d344713e0fa3ac20ac11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel-plugin/git/commits/b78feac448b71301481e54b60b93f6ad169d36a4","verification":{"payload":"tree e8ea7028f17ecd889074d344713e0fa3ac20ac11\nparent 0b5d075c63aabc38789931acccd16cbf5f1238e1\nauthor oulay2002 <41597851+oulay2002@users.noreply.github.com> 1790976411 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790976411 +0200\n\n[hooks] Detect the Vercel CLI on Windows (#143)\n\n* [hooks] Detect the Vercel CLI on Windows\n\nThe session-start profiler tells every Windows user to install a CLI they\nalready have. Two independent defects, both in the resolve-then-spawn path:\n\n1. `getBinaryPathCandidates` put the bare name ahead of every PATHEXT\n   suffix. npm lays down three entries per global binary in %APPDATA%\\npm:\n   `vercel` (a POSIX sh shim), `vercel.CMD` and `vercel.ps1`. The bare shim\n   won, and spawnSync rejects it with ENOENT.\n\n2. Even once `vercel.CMD` is selected, execFileSync cannot run it. Since the\n   fix for CVE-2024-27980, Node refuses .cmd/.bat without `shell: true`\n   (EINVAL). This hit the `npm view vercel version` probe too, so the\n   outdated-version branch was dead code on Windows.\n\nObserved on Windows 11, Node 24.18.0, with Vercel CLI 58.9.0 on PATH:\n\n    (no extension)  execFileSync -> ENOENT\n    .CMD            execFileSync -> EINVAL\n    .ps1            execFileSync -> EFTYPE\n\nOrder candidates by what Node can actually spawn (.EXE/.COM/.CMD/.BAT\nfirst, remaining PATHEXT entries next, bare name last), and route batch\nwrappers through the shell with the path quoted, since cmd.exe re-parses\nthe command line and would split an unquoted path on its spaces.\n\nAlso stop reporting `installed: false` when the binary resolved but the\nversion probe failed - the CLI is on PATH, and advising a reinstall is\nthe one answer that cannot help.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Run Windows batch wrappers from one quoted command string\n\nshell: true with an args array triggers Node 24''s DEP0190 warning on\nevery session start. Build a single command with the path quoted and\nrun it with execSync instead.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>