m/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel-gh-bot-3%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel-plugin/commits/3b7ad6f7c7bbc30990469467db4b454163aadd44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T19:27:55Z","email":"282332853+vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T19:27:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[skills] Sync turbopack with current docs (#260)\n\n* [skills] Sync turbopack with current docs\n\n<!-- vercel-plugin-drift-agent -->\n\n* fix(turbopack): register graphql-tag/loader via turbopack.rules\n\nNext.js lists graphql-tag/loader among loaders tested with Turbopack''s webpack loader implementation, which still requires registering it in turbopack.rules; it does not work with no config.\n\n* fix(turbopack): raw-loader runs through turbopack.rules too; the intro no longer says loaders are unsupported\n\nThe Next.js turbopack config page lists raw-loader among loaders tested with Turbopack''s webpack loader implementation and documents per-import turbopackLoader attributes (16.2.0). It supports a core subset of the loader API, only loaders that return JavaScript, and no webpack plugins. The old \"does not support webpack loaders directly\" intro contradicted the table.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: vercel-gh-bot-3[bot] <282332853+vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: molebox <rich@vercel.com>","tree":{"sha":"feabbcfb4f1f2cafdae39a149093765c264640e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel-plugin/git/trees/feabbcfb4f1f2cafdae39a149093765c264640e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel-plugin/git/commits/3b7ad6f7c7bbc30990469467db4b454163aadd44","verification":{"payload":"tree feabbcfb4f1f2cafdae39a149093765c264640e0\nparent b9f6f2aeb3bc99b7308b6dcf83d1324aa4b87da1\nauthor vercel-gh-bot-3[bot] <282332853+vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790364475 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790364475 +0200\n\n[skills] Sync turbopack with current docs (#260)\n\n* [skills] Sync turbopack with current docs\n\n<!-- vercel-plugin-drift-agent -->\n\n* fix(turbopack): register graphql-tag/loader via turbopack.rules\n\nNext.js lists graphql-tag/loader among loaders tested with Turbopack''s webpack loader implementation, which still requires registering it in turbopack.rules; it does not work with no config.\n\n* fix(turbopack): raw-loader runs through turbopack.rules too; the intro no longer says loaders are unsupported\n\nThe Next.js turbopack config page lists raw-loader among loaders tested with Turbopack''s webpack loader implementation and documents per-import turbopackLoader attributes (16.2.0). It supports a core subset of the loader API, only loaders that return JavaScript, and no webpack plugins. The old \"does not support webpack loaders directly\" intro contradicted the table.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: vercel-gh-bot-3[bot] <282332853+vercel-gh-bot-3[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: molebox <rich@vercel.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtss7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJiYQAJugPuFJNFXaw3AoNFPBpuxE\n80ShQvAf63CBcGoQtUORuiqbFZ/irwcMdDn9VrHtCrgKHAXKr1vfnRIrfaHukuB4\nA3P4O1j0e4wy7KlR1IoGvFtgwnLUd1fpY7ngoRxDears0ExYcL/0RNJBv37MEAiA\nG1Eq3Bct8IYEQKSjBXdp7dxaccguf9Z51YeYnjYu3UPKHpObayBC062jBkIfj8w9\nICQfTZvV5ox+O4YoNSAwxOtIXy8YWXpFe/GDExn7fuqpIQm91gPKNQdY3O8XbOJN\nMoGIFCxszgt0Lj+1ayJRn/PU+y/8aDyTmaGca1qWIqfnDVryH1EHEaSwx