de/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavovalverde/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavovalverde/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavovalverde/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gustavovalverde","id":16890942,"login":"gustavovalverde","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2ODkwOTQy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavovalverde/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavovalverde/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavovalverde/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavovalverde/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavovalverde/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gustavovalverde","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel-plugin/commits/74f7ddd1a5ca8965ff15d49d6e59c5c81c4c51be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T09:45:34Z","email":"g.valverde02@gmail.com","name":"Gustavo Valverde"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T09:45:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(env-vars): teach the Secret and Config variable types (#221)\n\n* fix(env-vars): teach the Secret and Config variable types\n\nThe skill still described the retired binary Sensitive model, so agents\nreached for --sensitive and the deprecated Enforce Sensitive policy.\nEnvironment variables are now typed Secret or Config: Secrets are\nhidden and replace-only, and Production and Preview Secrets are not\nreturned by vercel env pull.\n\n- Document the Secret and Config types, the non-interactive defaults,\n  and that public-prefixed variables such as NEXT_PUBLIC_* stay Config.\n- Use --type config|secret (Vercel CLI 59.6 and later), keeping\n  --visibility as its deprecated alias and --sensitive/--no-sensitive\n  as the legacy flags.\n- Replace the deprecated Enforce Sensitive Environment Variables policy\n  with Separate Production Secret Values.\n- Load the skill for vercel env update and vercel env run, and cover\n  both commands with pattern fixtures.\n- Regenerate commands/env.md, which includes the Add section.\n\n* fix(env-vars): add to several environments with a comma list; fold in #244''s scope and link fixes\n\n- `vercel env add NAME production preview` reads preview as a Git branch; use `production,preview`.\n- Production scope is the production domain, not only vercel.app.\n- Next.js environment variables link moved to /docs/app/guides/environment-variables.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: molebox <rich@vercel.com>","tree":{"sha":"de7b539e5fbacf8da48a0739e6193b0b9381cb90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel-plugin/git/trees/de7b539e5fbacf8da48a0739e6193b0b9381cb90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/vercel-plugin/git/commits/74f7ddd1a5ca8965ff15d49d6e59c5c81c4c51be","verification":{"payload":"tree de7b539e5fbacf8da48a0739e6193b0b9381cb90\nparent a59fbd16aa2da2421f098ecfa4200c1bce94aa33\nauthor Gustavo Valverde <g.valverde02@gmail.com> 1790329534 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790329534 +0200\n\nfix(env-vars): teach the Secret and Config variable types (#221)\n\n* fix(env-vars): teach the Secret and Config variable types\n\nThe skill still described the retired binary Sensitive model, so agents\nreached for --sensitive and the deprecated Enforce Sensitive policy.\nEnvironment variables are now typed Secret or Config: Secrets are\nhidden and replace-only, and Production and Preview Secrets are not\nreturned by vercel env pull.\n\n- Document the Secret and Config types, the non-interactive defaults,\n  and that public-prefixed variables such as NEXT_PUBLIC_* stay Config.\n- Use --type config|secret (Vercel CLI 59.6 and later), keeping\n  --visibility as its deprecated alias and --sensitive/--no-sensitive\n  as the legacy flags.\n- Replace the deprecated Enforce Sensitive Environment Variables policy\n  with Separate Production Secret Values.\n- Load the skill for vercel env update and vercel env run, and cover\n  both commands with pattern fixtures.\n- Regenerate commands/env.md, which includes the Add section.\n\n* fix(env-vars): add to several environments with a comma list; fold in #244''s scope and link fixes\n\n- `vercel env add NAME production preview` reads preview as a Git branch; use `production,preview`.\n- Production scope is the production domain, not only vercel.app.\n- Next.js environment variables link moved to /docs/app/guides/environment-variables.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: molebox <rich@vercel.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtkK+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4h4QABRL1hHKi5J4qvnzDmdqT14L\nuLFaAZARhfT6sF55zJzzyd8VIhtiqSj+4xIjrSHf2BNFMuqd7mhq4v4EsVIBiSz6\nvQLDTP4s6706lkmcS4Ezgir1/Bk3iFuHh7ZIstLAY/z+n5dv8tNUUT8CPpfPimkH\nTcBkfxtpZwqo4TJ+jWQ6eqzSmM7ecpX64iIkKFTUw0ErODtBlGtXUyeIZk9ix17K\nInDrzYCu3ypLphdEO8uk3JyITky0YF0Q4GBK3ALXc1xAaGWqSQ8Atp+Xbb2mXJTf\n+i1UlN0MZA4jiQmF8muId7XY7k4XxosseMrx/EHSdkJsVMvPlJrBAodPIPqP/I2U\nlruI1RJZTH8YiwMsgSPhq4zHkZu5GvL+dx9zMTCyR+pOOVX/4/2ZTBJJLtMX2B6q\nEmsNBW8n3QcjRtICxj4Rp82HM5WkxYBRBynSJK7T/AjR5hfjOj3sqeLjanyMNbAC\nu216HJHpnpAhNUlyF7myvCEiTsMx6NNqLZ4kFTsIG4UeY0b6Bsr9K5UsvmT7JWIx\nzy17GSmz1JnxSq+LwBxBdxkhv0uhGaTBneJ5oGYY7Cgn/H6VdMwetuu+2mPt7pgg\nwCl9VN8Ycn8nv2rerGYjr+oN37YXCtxWadousJArJ1J2RWmuGq28W0fb9czZ8Gq0\ncjJRJidgDhrJWxSGm6P3\n=Y6B6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T09:45:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-